-- A syntax error never reaches rustc, so it keeps its own `RDX` code rather
-- than acquiring one of rustc's.
--
-- The error was `print (1 +)` until doc 18 §4 made that a **left section**,
-- which parses and then fails in rustc — the opposite of what this asserts.
-- An unterminated group was tried next and is a *lexer* error (`RDX0012`),
-- not a parse one. A statement that begins with a binary operator has
-- nowhere left to go: `+` is not a prefix operator in any reading.
main :: ()
main =
  + 1
